Wait for a Vulkan present to complete before blitting an offscreen surface.

An offscreen client surface is not shown to the user by the present itself,
client_surface_present() blits it to the window afterwards. The OpenGL paths in
winex11 call glFinish() before that blit. The Vulkan path calls
client_surface_present() straight after vkQueuePresentKHR(), which only queues
the present, so the blit copies the frame before this one and the window keeps
showing it until something presents again. Fusion's viewport hits this: it
renders through DXVK into a child window, and a child window is always
composited offscreen.

VK_KHR_present_wait exists for this. Every present of an offscreen surface gets
an id and vkWaitForPresentKHR waits for that present before the blit. An
application that chains its own VkPresentIdKHR numbers its presents itself, so
win32u waits on those ids instead of adding a second struct, and the extensions
are only enabled when the application has not enabled them. Surfaces that are
not offscreen present to their window directly and are never waited for. The
timeout only guards against a present that never completes.

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
